        "response": {
          "bodySize": 22310,
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "size": 22310,
            "text": "{\"sha\":\"c77869250658d76a185813ac186914c14dccbc7e\",\"parents\":[\"543b8db50a839029b03d7ca7957884d806df646c\"],\"message\":\"refactor: bind hello-mcp from task.toml and fix the eval run invocation (#15)\\n\\n* fix: commit a loopback hello-mcp binding for platform eval trials\\n\\nA platform eval trial reads the Recipe's committed .pi/mcp.local.json, so the\\nsidecar world needs the file in the checkout. Recipe validation accepts a\\ncommitted binding only to a loopback URL, so it names localhost:8000, which\\nreaches the sidecar through the pod's shared network namespace.\\n\\nrun-local.sh swaps the compose-name binding in for a local Docker trial, where\\nmcp-server is a separate container, and restores the committed file on exit.\\ndocs/mcp-bindings.md explains how the id is bound in each world.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* chore: align .gitignore with the recipe template\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* chore: remove the token-bearing remote MCP binding example\\n\\nA credential-bearing binding belongs outside the repository; run-local.sh\\ntakes its path through HELLO_MCP_BINDING.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* docs: call out task.toml's mcp_servers declaration and its status\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* Revert \\\"chore: remove the token-bearing remote MCP binding example\\\"\\n\\nThis reverts commit 950c834a66c5fa979fd57c4d098d3e5d9f0d5c81.\\n\\n* docs: document the remote example as a run-local.sh binding\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* refactor: simplify run-local.sh and document both local runs\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* fix: pass --path and --runtime to introspection eval run\\n\\nCLI 0.60 rejects a positional task path, and two Runtime manifests share this\\ndirectory, so a run must name one.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* refactor: bind hello-mcp from task.toml through the Harbor adapter\\n\\nThe Introspection Harbor adapter writes a task's [[environment.mcp_servers]]\\ninto the Recipe's .pi/mcp.local.json on every run, local and platform, so the\\ncommitted loopback binding and run-local.sh's copy were redundant. Drop both\\nand the sidecar example, ignore .pi/mcp.local.json again, and document the\\nrule: name is the Recipe's MCP id, the URL host is the compose service name.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* docs: add a localhost example binding for introspection local\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n---------\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-10-28T15:17:43-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-10-28T15:17:43-07:00\"},\"files\":[{\"filename\":\".gitignore\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":16,\"deletions\":4,\"changes\":20},{\"filename\":\".introspection/hello-mcp-local.yaml\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":2,\"deletions\":2,\"changes\":4},{\"filename\":\".pi/mcp.local.example.json\",\"status\":\"renamed\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":1,\"changes\":2},{\"filename\":\"README.md\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":77,\"deletions\":43,\"changes\":120},{\"filename\":\"docs/mcp-bindings.md\",\"status\":\"added\",\"additions\":77,\"deletions\":0,\"changes\":77},{\"filename\":\"harbor/task.toml\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":3,\"deletions\":4,\"changes\":7},{\"filename\":\"scripts/deploy-runtime.sh\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":2,\"deletions\":2,\"changes\":4},{\"filename\":\"scripts/run-local.sh\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":13,\"changes\":18}],\"patch\":\"diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore\\nindex 3729477..0f1143d 100644\\n--- a/.gitignore\\n+++ b/.gitignore\\n@@ -1,8 +1,20 @@\\n-node_modules/\\n+# Generated Pi runtime state\\n+.pi/bin/\\n+.pi/mcp-session.json\\n+.pi/mcporter.json\\n .pi/mcp-catalogs/\\n .introspection/local.json\\n-.env\\n-.env.*\\n+\\n+# Local MCP binding: a Harbor trial writes it from task.toml; for\\n+# `introspection local`, copy in one of the .pi/*.example.json files.\\n+.pi/mcp.local.json\\n+\\n+# Dependencies\\n+node_modules/\\n __pycache__/\\n *.pyc\\n-.pi/mcp.local.json\\n+\\n+# Secrets. `introspection dev` stages with `git add -A`, so anything untracked\\n+# and un-ignored here travels to the cloud inside the development patch.\\n+.env\\n+.env.*\\ndiff --git a/.introspection/hello-mcp-local.yaml b/.introspection/hello-mcp-local.yaml\\nindex 56c694e..49b5e99 100644\\n--- a/.introspection/hello-mcp-local.yaml\\n+++ b/.introspection/hello-mcp-local.yaml\\n@@ -3,5 +3,5 @@ path: .\\n description: Harbor task calling the hello MCP as a compose sidecar of the trial\\n runtime:\\n   llm_mode: managed\\n-  # No connector: the Recipe's hello-mcp id resolves to the sidecar through\\n-  # the committed .pi/mcp.local.json binding, so the world is inside the task.\\n+  # No connector: a Harbor trial binds the Recipe's hello-mcp id to the\\n+  # task's mcp-server sidecar from task.toml, so the world is inside the task.\\ndiff --git a/.pi/mcp.sidecar.example.json b/.pi/mcp.local.example.json\\nsimilarity index 70%\\nrename from .pi/mcp.sidecar.example.json\\nrename to .pi/mcp.local.example.json\\nindex a0dadb4..0bc8a34 100644\\n--- a/.pi/mcp.sidecar.example.json\\n+++ b/.pi/mcp.local.example.json\\n@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@\\n     {\\n       \\\"id\\\": \\\"hello-mcp\\\",\\n       \\\"transport\\\": \\\"streamable_http\\\",\\n-      \\\"url\\\": \\\"http://mcp-server:8000/mcp\\\"\\n+      \\\"url\\\": \\\"http://localhost:8000/mcp\\\"\\n     }\\n   ]\\n }\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex 7d8703c..8043910 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -30,7 +30,8 @@ harbor/                                the Harbor task, laid out as harbor/examp\\n └── tests/test.sh                      Harbor's verifier: reads /tmp/greeting.txt\\n judges/greeting.yaml                   the same check as tests/test.sh, over the trajectory\\n agents/agent.yaml                      the Recipe agent; uses `hello-mcp` `echo`\\n-.pi/mcp.sidecar.example.json           binds `hello-mcp` → http://mcp-server:8000/mcp (copy to .pi/mcp.local.json)\\n+.pi/mcp.local.example.json             binds `hello-mcp` → http://localhost:8000/mcp (`introspection local`)\\n+.pi/mcp.remote.example.json            binds `hello-mcp` → the public server, token from HELLO_MCP_TOKEN (`introspection local`)\\n .introspection/hello-mcp-local.yaml    Runtime manifest for the sidecar world\\n .introspection/hello-mcp.yaml          Runtime manifest for the remote world (connector)\\n ```\\n@@ -49,37 +50,59 @@ pull from. See introspection-cloud `docs/design/eval-task-sidecars.md`.\\n \\n ### How `hello-mcp` resolves\\n \\n-The Recipe's `package.json` declares `hello-mcp` as a required MCP server. Two\\n-bindings can satisfy it:\\n-\\n-1. A local binding file, `.pi/mcp.local.json`, points it at\\n-   `http://mcp-server:8000/mcp`. That URL is the compose service name, which\\n-   resolves inside a Harbor trial and inside the sandbox pod alike. The file is\\n-   local capability configuration, which `recipes check` refuses to see\\n-   committed, so it ships as `.pi/mcp.sidecar.example.json` and is copied into\\n-   place for a local run:\\n-\\n-   ```sh\\n-   cp .pi/mcp.sidecar.example.json .pi/mcp.local.json\\n-   ```\\n-\\n-   On the platform the same binding has to reach the sandbox with the task,\\n-   derived from `task.toml`'s `[[environment.mcp_servers]]`, whose `url` names\\n-   a compose service. That is a follow-up on the task adapter and the runtime\\n-   (see the pull request); until it lands, a platform trial in the sidecar\\n-   world resolves `hello-mcp` only if the Runtime carries a binding for it.\\n-2. A Runtime with the `hello-mcp` connector bound resolves it to the public\\n-   server at egress. A cloud binding wins over the local file, so deploying the\\n-   Recipe as the `hello-mcp` Runtime (with its connector) is what selects the\\n-   remote world; deploying it as `hello-mcp-local` keeps the sidecar.\\n-\\n-For a direct local run against the public server without the platform, use the\\n-token-bearing example instead:\\n+The Recipe's `package.json` declares `hello-mcp` as a required MCP server. A\\n+Harbor trial binds it from the task itself, in `harbor/task.toml`:\\n+\\n+```toml\\n+[[environment.mcp_servers]]\\n+name = \\\"hello-mcp\\\"                  # the MCP server id the Recipe declares\\n+transport = \\\"streamable-http\\\"       # the only transport a Recipe binds\\n+url = \\\"http://mcp-server:8000/mcp\\\"  # the compose service name from docker-compose.yaml\\n+```\\n+\\n+Before the agent starts, the Introspection Harbor adapter writes these entries\\n+into the Recipe's `.pi/mcp.local.json` inside the trial, replacing anything the\\n+checkout carried. That happens on every Harbor run, local or on the platform,\\n+so the task is the single place the binding lives. See\\n+[docs/mcp-bindings.md](docs/mcp-bindings.md).\\n+\\n+The rule to follow: **`name` is the Recipe's MCP server id, and the `url` host\\n+is the service's name in `docker-compose.yaml`.** That name resolves in both\\n+places the task runs:\\n+\\n+- **Local Docker trial:** Docker Compose's DNS resolves each service name on the\\n+  compose network.\\n+- **Platform eval trial:** every compose service runs as a sidecar of the\\n+  sandbox pod, and the platform resolves each service name to the pod's\\n+  loopback, so the same URL connects unchanged.\\n+\\n+`localhost` would work on the platform only, since under Docker Compose it\\n+names the agent's own container.\\n+\\n+`introspection local` runs the Recipe on your machine, outside Harbor, and\\n+reads `.pi/mcp.local.json`, which is git-ignored. Copy in the example for the\\n+server you want.\\n+\\n+Against the hello server on your machine:\\n \\n ```sh\\n-cp .pi/mcp.remote.example.json .pi/mcp.local.json   # fill in HELLO_MCP_TOKEN\\n+pip install \\\"fastmcp>=2.0,<3\\\"\\n+python harbor/environment/mcp-server/server.py &       # serves http://localhost:8000/mcp\\n+cp .pi/mcp.local.example.json .pi/mcp.local.json\\n+introspection local --runtime hello-mcp-local\\n ```\\n \\n+Against the authenticated public server:\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+export HELLO_MCP_TOKEN=...\\n+cp .pi/mcp.remote.example.json .pi/mcp.local.json\\n+introspection local --runtime hello-mcp\\n+```\\n+\\n+The remote example carries a `${HELLO_MCP_TOKEN}` reference, never a token.\\n+A Harbor run ignores both files: it binds from `task.toml`.\\n+\\n ## The four ways to run this\\n \\n Same instruction, same Recipe, same judge — five places the trial can run. Only\\n@@ -91,8 +114,8 @@ and the commands surface through the raw API, which is what\\n | Shape | Script | Where the trial runs | How `hello-mcp` resolves |\\n | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n | Local Docker | `./scripts/run-local.sh` | Harbor's Docker provider on your machine | `mcp-server` compose container; direct model + MCP calls from your keys |\\n-| Platform, sidecar | `introspection eval run harbor` | in-cluster sandbox pod | `mcp-server` as a pod sidecar on loopback; its image built through `/v1/images` |\\n-| Platform, remote | `introspection eval run harbor` | any provider, including E2B | the Runtime's connector binding; credential injected at egress |\\n+| Platform, sidecar | `introspection eval run --path harbor --runtime hello-mcp-local --runtime-version <id>` | in-cluster sandbox pod | `mcp-server` as a pod sidecar on loopback; its image built through `/v1/images` |\\n+| Platform, remote | `introspection eval run --path harbor --runtime hello-mcp --runtime-version <id>` | any provider, including E2B | the Runtime's connector binding; credential injected at egress |\\n | E2B, host-driven | `./scripts/run-e2b.sh` | E2B sandbox, Harbor drives it from your machine | the Runtime's connector binding under managed egress, or `HELLO_MCP_TOKEN` |\\n | Platform, contract check | `./scripts/run-eval-compose.sh` | in-cluster sandbox pod | `mcp-server` as a sidecar, built and addressed through the raw API rather than the adapter |\\n \\n@@ -114,9 +137,9 @@ digest pinning, scanning, content-dedup and provenance.\\n ### Order of operations\\n \\n ```sh\\n-./scripts/deploy-runtime.sh          # 1. a Runtime version, baked\\n-./scripts/setup-introspection.sh     # 2. connector + binding (remote/E2B worlds only)\\n-introspection eval run harbor        # 3. run\\n+version=$(./scripts/deploy-runtime.sh)   # 1. a Runtime version, baked; prints its id\\n+./scripts/setup-introspection.sh         # 2. connector + binding (remote/E2B worlds only)\\n+introspection eval run --path harbor --runtime hello-mcp-local --runtime-version \\\"$version\\\"   # 3. run\\n ```\\n \\n `deploy-runtime.sh` takes `--manifest` to choose the world:\\n@@ -133,20 +156,23 @@ as the context upload and fails there.\\n \\n ## Run locally with Harbor\\n \\n-Install the Harbor tooling, then run the task on Harbor's Docker provider,\\n-which builds `mcp-server` from `harbor/environment/mcp-server/` and starts it beside the agent:\\n+`./scripts/run-local.sh` runs the task on Harbor's own Docker provider, with no\\n+Introspection plane involved: Docker Compose builds and starts `main` (the\\n+agent) and `mcp-server`, the agent calls your model provider directly, and\\n+Harbor's verifier (`tests/test.sh`) checks the result. A failure here is the\\n+task's or the Recipe's, not the platform's.\\n+\\n+You need Docker, Node.js 24 or newer, the Introspection CLI\\n+(`npm install -g @introspection-ai/cli`) and your model key (for example\\n+`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`) in the environment. The script runs `introspection setup\\n+--target harbor` for you.\\n \\n ```sh\\n ./scripts/run-local.sh\\n ```\\n \\n-which is `introspection setup --target harbor` plus `introspection eval run\\n-harbor`, with the `.pi/mcp.local.json` binding copied into place first — the\\n-one step that is easy to forget, since the file is git-ignored and the Recipe\\n-declares `hello-mcp` as required.\\n-\\n-The bootstrap adapter installs the Recipe into `main`; the sidecar is reached at\\n-`http://mcp-server:8000/mcp` exactly as the compose file says.\\n+The adapter binds `hello-mcp` to `http://mcp-server:8000/mcp` from\\n+`task.toml`, so nothing needs copying into place first.\\n \\n ## Run as an eval task on the platform\\n \\n@@ -163,9 +189,17 @@ is `@/workspace/files/instruction.md`, the runtime takes the one turn from the\\n spawn env, judges the conversation when it settles, posts the result and ends.\\n \\n ```sh\\n-introspection eval run harbor\\n+export INTROSPECTION_DP_URL=...    # the data plane's API URL\\n+export INTROSPECTION_TOKEN=...     # project API key with the `evals` and `runtimes` capabilities\\n+version=$(./scripts/deploy-runtime.sh)\\n+introspection eval run --path harbor --runtime hello-mcp-local --runtime-version \\\"$version\\\"\\n ```\\n \\n+`--runtime` names the manifest and `--runtime-version` the deployed version\\n+`deploy-runtime.sh` prints, so the run makes no Control Plane request and needs\\n+no `introspection login`. The adapter binds `hello-mcp` from `task.toml` here\\n+too.\\n+\\n The environment sends the compose file as the task's `compose` field, minus\\n `build`:\\n \\ndiff --git a/docs/mcp-bindings.md b/docs/mcp-bindings.md\\nnew file mode 100644\\nindex 0000000..42fe081\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/docs/mcp-bindings.md\\n@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@\\n+# How `hello-mcp` is bound\\n+\\n+This Recipe declares one logical MCP server, `hello-mcp`, as required in\\n+`package.json`. The agent (`agents/agent.yaml`) only ever names that id. Which\\n+server the id reaches is a *binding*, and for a Harbor trial the binding is\\n+declared by the task, not the Recipe.\\n+\\n+## The task declares the binding\\n+\\n+`harbor/task.toml`:\\n+\\n+```toml\\n+[[environment.mcp_servers]]\\n+name = \\\"hello-mcp\\\"\\n+transport = \\\"streamable-http\\\"\\n+url = \\\"http://mcp-server:8000/mcp\\\"\\n+```\\n+\\n+- `name` is the MCP server id the Recipe declares.\\n+- `transport` must be `streamable-http`; a Recipe binds nothing else.\\n+- The URL's host is the service's name in `harbor/environment/docker-compose.yaml`.\\n+\\n+Before the agent starts, the Introspection Harbor adapter writes these entries\\n+into the Recipe's `.pi/mcp.local.json` inside the trial. It does this on every\\n+Harbor run, local or on the platform, and replaces anything the checkout\\n+carried. Nothing needs committing or copying into place.\\n+\\n+## Why the compose service name\\n+\\n+The same URL has to work in both places the task runs:\\n+\\n+| Where | How `mcp-server` resolves |\\n+| --- | --- |\\n+| Local Harbor Docker trial (`scripts/run-local.sh`) | Docker Compose's DNS resolves each service name on the compose network |\\n+| Platform eval trial | Each compose service runs as a sidecar of the sandbox pod, and the platform resolves each service name to the pod's loopback |\\n+\\n+`localhost` works on the platform only: under Docker Compose it names the\\n+agent's own container.\\n+\\n+On the platform, sidecars start before the agent in `depends_on` order, and the\\n+agent starts only once their healthchecks pass. Compose sidecars need a\\n+Kubernetes sandbox, so a task with a compose world always runs in-cluster.\\n+\\n+## Outside Harbor\\n+\\n+`introspection local` runs the Recipe on your machine, outside Harbor, and\\n+reads `.pi/mcp.local.json`, which is git-ignored. Copy in the example for the\\n+server you want.\\n+\\n+Against the hello server on your machine:\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+pip install \\\"fastmcp>=2.0,<3\\\"\\n+python harbor/environment/mcp-server/server.py &       # serves http://localhost:8000/mcp\\n+cp .pi/mcp.local.example.json .pi/mcp.local.json\\n+introspection local --runtime hello-mcp-local\\n+```\\n+\\n+Against the authenticated public server:\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+export HELLO_MCP_TOKEN=...\\n+cp .pi/mcp.remote.example.json .pi/mcp.local.json\\n+introspection local --runtime hello-mcp\\n+```\\n+\\n+The remote example carries a `${HELLO_MCP_TOKEN}` reference, never a token.\\n+A Harbor run ignores both files: it binds from `task.toml`.\\n+\\n+## Connector world\\n+\\n+A Runtime deployed from `.introspection/hello-mcp.yaml` has a `hello-mcp`\\n+connector. Its binding resolves the id to the authenticated public server, and\\n+the credential is injected at egress rather than placed in the sandbox. A\\n+non-Harbor task on that Runtime (`introspection tasks create`) uses it. A\\n+Harbor trial binds `hello-mcp` from `task.toml` instead, since the adapter's\\n+binding wins on an eval task.\\ndiff --git a/harbor/task.toml b/harbor/task.toml\\nindex b97b0df..7d799aa 100644\\n--- a/harbor/task.toml\\n+++ b/harbor/task.toml\\n@@ -18,10 +18,9 @@ cpus = 1\\n memory_mb = 2048\\n storage_mb = 10240\\n \\n-# The world's MCP server, by its compose service name. Locally the Recipe\\n-# binds its `hello-mcp` id to this URL through .pi/mcp.local.json (copied from\\n-# .pi/mcp.sidecar.example.json); a Runtime with the hello-mcp connector bound\\n-# resolves the same id to the public server instead.\\n+# The Recipe's `hello-mcp` server, bound by the Harbor adapter on every run.\\n+# `name` is the Recipe's MCP server id; the URL's host is the compose service\\n+# name, which resolves under Docker Compose and in the platform's sandbox pod.\\n [[environment.mcp_servers]]\\n name = \\\"hello-mcp\\\"\\n transport = \\\"streamable-http\\\"\\ndiff --git a/scripts/deploy-runtime.sh b/scripts/deploy-runtime.sh\\nindex cbd934b..08da64d 100755\\n--- a/scripts/deploy-runtime.sh\\n+++ b/scripts/deploy-runtime.sh\\n@@ -12,11 +12,11 @@\\n #\\n #   hello-mcp-local.yaml  the sidecar world. No connector: the MCP is a compose\\n #                         service of the task, reached on the pod's loopback.\\n-#                         Pair with `introspection eval run harbor`.\\n+#                         Pair with `introspection eval run --path harbor --runtime-version`.\\n #   hello-mcp.yaml        the connector world. The Runtime carries the hello-mcp\\n #                         binding and the credential is injected at egress, so\\n #                         nothing on the host holds a token. Pair with\\n-#                         `run-e2b.sh`, or `introspection eval run harbor`.\\n+#                         `run-e2b.sh`, or `introspection eval run --path harbor --runtime-version`.\\n #\\n # The connector itself, its authorization and the MCP binding are\\n # `setup-introspection.sh`'s job, and only the connector world needs them.\\ndiff --git a/scripts/run-local.sh b/scripts/run-local.sh\\nindex 5a691c2..238910e 100755\\n--- a/scripts/run-local.sh\\n+++ b/scripts/run-local.sh\\n@@ -9,11 +9,8 @@\\n # uploads an image, creates a task, or needs a credential beyond the model key\\n # the agent uses — so a failure here is the task's, not the platform's.\\n #\\n-# The one step that is easy to forget is the MCP binding: the Recipe declares\\n-# `hello-mcp` as a required server, and `.pi/mcp.local.json` is what points\\n-# that id somewhere. It is git-ignored (it is local capability configuration,\\n-# which `recipes check` refuses to see committed), so it ships as an example\\n-# and is copied into place here.\\n+# The Harbor adapter binds the Recipe's `hello-mcp` from task.toml's\\n+# [[environment.mcp_servers]], so there is no binding file to put in place.\\n \\n set -eu\\n \\n@@ -23,14 +20,9 @@ if [ \\\"$#\\\" -ne 0 ]; then\\n fi\\n \\n task=${HELLO_MCP_TASK:-harbor}\\n-binding=${HELLO_MCP_BINDING:-.pi/mcp.sidecar.example.json}\\n-\\n-if [ ! -f .pi/mcp.local.json ]; then\\n-  echo \\\"Binding hello-mcp from $binding\\\" >&2\\n-  cp \\\"$binding\\\" .pi/mcp.local.json\\n-fi\\n \\n # `eval run` infers the runner from the path: a directory holding task.toml is\\n-# a Harbor task, so the runner never has to be named.\\n+# a Harbor task. `--runtime` is required because two manifests share this\\n+# directory; both describe the same Recipe, so either serves a local run.\\n introspection setup --target harbor --yes\\n-exec introspection eval run \\\"$task\\\"\\n+exec introspection eval run --path \\\"$task\\\" --runtime hello-mcp-local\\n\"}"
          },
